//@version=6
indicator("vw-udt-legacy-array-param", overlay = false)

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-16 by the UDT coverage unit for queue row UDT-T1
// (docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-16-udt.md). No licence-held text. Never compiled on TradingView: a line
// that does not compile IS the reading (record its text).
// QUESTION: a user function parameter typed with the legacy `T[]` spelling (`float[] a`, `int[] a`). Our runtime
// lane refuses it (`runtime:function`, "a parameter this front end cannot read (`[`)"). Does v6 compile it, and
// is it the same parameter as `array<T> a` (T01 = the size, 3; T02 = the element, 5)?
// CAPTURE: NYSE:RDDT 1D from the listing, inputs at defaults (none), AFTER THE CLOSE. A00 is the control.
plot(bar_index, "A00_bar_index_CONTROL")

f(float[] a) =>
    array.size(a)
plot(f(array.from(1.0, 2.0, close)), "T01_size_through_float_legacy_param")

g(int[] a, int i) =>
    array.get(a, i)
plot(g(array.from(4, 5, 6), 1), "T02_get_through_int_legacy_param")
